# Citation metadata for SONARITHM.
# Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# GitHub renders this file as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads it when archiving releases.
# Completed in roadmap phase A07 (first release and Zenodo DOI). See docs/engineering/release-process.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SONARITHM in your work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: SONARITHM
abstract: >-
  SONARITHM is an open-source application and framework that turns graphs,
  charts and numerical data into structured, navigable sound. A declarative
  sonification specification is compiled into a canonical intermediate
  representation (the Score) and rendered by one deterministic Rust core, which
  is shared by a desktop application (Tauri 2 with React Aria), a command-line
  tool and Python bindings. Its design defaults are traced to published
  auditory-display and accessibility research, and its interface is designed to
  be used by blind and low-vision people with their own assistive technology.
  Renders carry provenance (engine version, spec hash and data fingerprint) so
  that results can be reproduced.
authors:
  # TODO: add given-names, family-names, ORCID
  - alias: "DuhItzAniket"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DuhItzAniket/SONARITHM"
keywords:
  - sonification
  - auditory display
  - auditory graphs
  - parameter mapping sonification
  - data accessibility
  - blind and low vision
  - screen reader
  - data visualization
  - reproducible research
  - research software
  - Rust
# license: omitted until ADR-0010 (licensing) is accepted. ADR-0010 proposes MIT OR Apache-2.0.
#   When accepted, list both SPDX identifiers: license: [MIT, Apache-2.0]
#   (the CFF 1.2.0 schema reads a list of licences as OR, not AND).
version: "0.0.0"
# date-released: omitted until the first tagged release (v0.1.0-alpha, phase A07).
# doi: add the Zenodo concept DOI after the first release is archived (phase A07).
